723:4. **Methodological:** Bootstrap BCa CIs (200 resamples) provide a non-parametric check on normal-approximation CIs (§9.2.2; caveat: B = 200 is underpowered, §9.2 #15); paired-difference bootstrap (B = 2000, §8.6) confirms the normal-approximation CIs within $0.30; seed-count convergence diagnostic shows `cam_multisignal` and ρ stable from 20 seeds (§9.2.2; caveat: N = 10 is vacuously stable and the path is non-monotone, §9.2 #17); macro-F1 (§8.9) provides per-class F1 beyond raw match accuracy; common random numbers (§8.9) confirm CRN changes profits by <$3 and does not affect conclusions; all p-values survive Bonferroni correction (§7.3). v1.3 extensions (§8.10–§8.17) add 8 ablations: adversarial mapping, channel-dependent reward, bandit baselines, class-conditional noise, convergence trend, perception dose-response, crisis bid policy, and sensing fidelity. v1.4 extensions (§8.18–§8.20) add online reward-feedback learning (UCB1 recovers 83.0% of the fixed-mapping value with zero labeled action data; F10), a mid-episode drift condition (post-drift recalibration is net-negative; multi-signal inference is drift-robust), and flat-taxonomy confusion quantification (intent-only 11.0% cross-axis confusion vs 1.0% multi-signal). The v1.5 extension (§8.21) adds the pre-registered LLM zero-shot classification baseline (API models at temperature 0: 79.9–83.0% accuracy; F11). Note: ρ(match rate, profit) is an environment-consistency check, not a dose-response law — the match bonus is a linear component of profit (§9.2 #11).
